    "title": "15-year-old dies in dirt bike crash east of Colorado Springs - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ashley Eberhardt ,\n1 hours ago\n(EL PASO COUNTY, Colo.) — A 15-year-old boy has died after a crash involving two dirt bikes near Ellicott on Christmas Eve, Dec. 24.\nAccording to the Colorado State Patrol (CSP), around 5 p.m., CSP responded to the area of South Ellicott Highway and Jayhawk Avenue on a report of a crash involving two dirt bikes.\nCSP said each dirt bike was ridden by a single person: a 15-year-old boy and a 21-year-old man. First responders attempted life-saving measures on both dirt bike riders while awaiting a medical helicopter; however, the 15-year-old was pronounced dead on the scene.\nThe 21-year-old was flown by helicopter to the hospital.\nCSP said no cause for the crash has been determined yet, though the investigation is ongoing.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX21 News Colorado.",
